  <h2>The Problem</h2>
  <p>
    The EPA has documented indoor air as 2–5x more polluted than outdoor air in the average
    American home. Volatile organic compounds (VOCs) off-gas continuously from furniture,
    flooring, paint, and cleaning products. Cooking generates particulate matter that lingers
    for hours. Mold spores from hidden moisture colonize HVAC systems and release mycotoxins
    that act as direct neurotoxins. You breathe this mix all night while your brain is
    supposedly recovering.
  </p>
  <p>
    Mycotoxin exposure is particularly underestimated. Even at subclinical levels, mold-derived
    toxins impair cognitive function, disrupt the HPA axis, and generate chronic inflammatory
    load that compounds with every other stressor in the 4M profile. Most men with persistent
    brain fog, fatigue, and unexplained mood disruption have never been assessed for this.
  </p>
  <p>
    The intervention isn't complicated. A quality HEPA + activated carbon filtration unit in
    the bedroom — where you spend the most concentrated time breathing — is the highest-ROI
    environmental upgrade most people haven't made.
  </p>

  <h2>The Insulting Behaviors</h2>
  <ul class="insult-list">
    <li>No air filtration in the bedroom — breathing unfiltered indoor air during your 7–8 hour recovery window</li>
    <li>HVAC filters changed less than quarterly — the system distributes whatever has accumulated in the filter</li>
    <li>Cooking without ventilation — gas stoves produce NO₂ and particulates that can linger for hours</li>
    <li>Sealing the home in winter without any fresh air exchange — VOC levels spike in sealed spaces</li>
    <li>Ignoring visible mold or musty odors — the visible is always a fraction of the biological load present</li>
    <li>Synthetic air fresheners and candles — primary VOC source in many homes</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 class="section-eliminate">Eliminate the Insulting Behavior</h2>
  <div class="card-grid">
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Step 1 — Bedroom HEPA + Carbon Unit</h3>
      <p>A properly-sized HEPA + activated carbon air purifier running in your bedroom while you sleep. This is the single most impactful air quality intervention available.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Step 2 — Change HVAC Filters Every 90 Days</h3>
      <p>MERV-13 filters at minimum. Set a recurring calendar reminder. This is the most commonly neglected maintenance task with the most widespread impact.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Step 3 — Mold Testing If Symptoms Match</h3>
      <p>Brain fog, fatigue, chronic congestion, and mood disruption that don't respond to other interventions — get a professional mold inspection and ERMI test.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Step 4 — Source Control</h3>
      <p>Replace synthetic air fresheners, conventional cleaning products, and scented candles with unscented or naturally-scented alternatives. Remove the VOC sources before filtering them.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

